<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- Portrait status bar. 45dp, not the 40dp Stock reserves, and the
         difference is load-bearing.

         The punch hole was measured at y 12..70 display pixels, so the bar has
         to be at least 70px tall to clear it. dp are resolved against the
         *runtime* density, not ro.sf.lcd_density:

             density 320 (default)                  45dp = 90px   clears 70
             density 256 (owner's Display Size)     45dp = 72px   clears 70
             density 256 with the old 40dp          40dp = 64px   DOES NOT clear

         The owner runs Display Size at "small", i.e. display_density_forced=256.
         At that density the previous 40dp rendered a 64px bar, narrower than the
         aperture. Apps stayed safe either way, because
         DisplayPolicy.getStatusBarHeight() takes the max of this dimen and the
         cutout's safe inset and so clamped to 70 - but SystemUI's own status
         icons are laid out inside this dimen, so they had no margin below the
         hole and the clock sat against it. 45dp is the smallest value that
         clears 70px at both densities.

         Upper bound: it must stay at or below the 48dp quick_qs_offset_height
         default, or the Quick Settings header needs a matching override. 45dp
         does, with 3dp to spare.

         (An earlier revision of this comment described the 40dp case and is
         wrong; notes/HANDOFF.md's "display_density_forced=256 is not a defect"
         entry described the same 64px situation as an accepted cost, which it no
         longer is.) -->
    <dimen name="status_bar_height_portrait">45dp</dimen>

    <!-- Landscape. Rotating the device moves the hole to a *side* edge, so there
         is nothing above the content to clear and the bar does not need to grow;
         Stock's 40dp landscape bar just spends 40dp of a 720px-tall viewport for
         nothing.

         AOSP defaults this to @dimen/status_bar_height_portrait
         (frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/dimens.xml), so leaving it unset
         would inherit the 45dp above. It is restated here at 25dp - AOSP's own
         24dp landscape convention plus 1dp, which keeps it a hair above the
         status bar content height at density 256 (25dp = 40px). -->
    <dimen name="status_bar_height_landscape">25dp</dimen>
</resources>
